# Frontend clickables

When adding or changing any clickable control in the frontend:

- Use `Button` from `frontend/src/components/ui` (or `buttonClasses` for `Link`-styled actions).
- Do **not** use raw `<button>` for UI actions — that skips shared styles like `cursor-pointer`.
- For icon-only controls (edit/delete/add), use `size="icon"`.
- Default size is `md` (filled pill). Prefer existing variants: `primary`, `secondary`, `ghost`, `danger`.

## Cursor pointer (required)

Anything the user can click/tap must show `cursor: pointer` on hover:

- Buttons, links, icon actions, tabs, cards with `onClick` / `role="link"` / `role="button"`
- Menu items, checkboxes/radio labels that act as controls
- Disabled controls use `cursor-not-allowed` (never pointer)

If a custom clickable cannot use `Button`, add `cursor-pointer` (or ensure the global clickable base styles cover it). Never leave interactive elements on the default arrow cursor.
